---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const steps = [
  ['Consent', 'Nothing about your company goes to a buyer until an authorised person at your company agrees, in writing, to an introduction.'],
  ['Inventory', 'You list the records you hold, who owns them, and the restrictions attached to each set. We help you decide which sets to consider. There is no obligation to proceed.'],
  ['Introduction', 'We introduce you to a buyer that licenses data for AI training, such as micro1 or Polyshares. You can speak to more than one.'],
  ['Contract', 'You review the licensing agreement directly with the buyer: the exact records, de-identification, permitted uses, recipients, access controls, payment and withdrawal terms. You decide whether to sign.'],
  ['Delivery and payment', 'Records move directly between you and the buyer, within the scope written into the contract. The buyer pays you under the agreed terms.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Operating records" description="Decide whether to license your operating records for AI training, with an inventory, clear boundaries and redaction before delivery.">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Operating records · Plate 05</span>
    <h1>The work you already know how to do has a second use.</h1>
    <p class="lede">AI labs buy records of how real businesses work. We help you decide what you can license, what must stay private, and whether the terms make sense for you.</p>
    <a class="link-rule" href="mailto:m@statecraft.systems?subject=Records%20review">Book a 20-minute records review</a>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap split" aria-labelledby="for-h">
    <div class="left"><span class="eyebrow">01 · Who it's for</span><h2 id="for-h">Businesses with a record of real work.</h2></div>
    <div class="right prose">
      <h2>Operating companies</h2>
      <p>Companies with 30 or more staff and mature internal documentation. Typical examples: staffing and recruiting firms, call centres and BPO providers, insurance agencies, outsourced accounting firms, and managed service providers (MSPs).</p>
      <p>The useful material records how your team handles a request, makes a decision, checks quality or resolves a problem. It does not need to be polished for publication.</p>
      <h2>What qualifies</h2>
      <p>Internal SOPs, ticket histories, CRM notes, call scripts and QA rubrics can qualify when you own the rights to license them and they can be cleaned safely.</p>
      <h2>What doesn't</h2>
      <p>Client-owned records and contract-restricted material are excluded. So are personal details, client names, credentials, and anything a regulator protects. Removing a name does not create a right to license a record you do not own.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="records-band" aria-labelledby="process-h">
    <div class="wrap records">
      <div class="records-heading"><span class="eyebrow">02 · How it works</span><h2 id="process-h">Five steps. You decide what moves.</h2></div>
      <ol class="records-list">
        {steps.map(([title, text], index) => <li><span class="record-num" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div></li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap split" aria-labelledby="closed-h">
    <div class="left"><span class="eyebrow">03 · Closed or winding down</span><h2 id="closed-h">When the company has stopped trading.</h2></div>
    <div class="right prose">
      <p>For founders, trustees, assignees for the benefit of creditors (ABC assignees) and restructuring counsel handling a company that has closed or is winding down.</p>
      <p>What buyers look for: companies that had 50 or more staff at their peak, with Slack or Teams history and internal documents, licensed as a de-identified archive.</p>
      <p>Only the person with legal authority over the records can agree to a sale. In a bankruptcy estate that is the trustee or debtor in possession, and the sale needs court approval.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap split" aria-labelledby="fee-h">
    <div class="left"><span class="eyebrow">04 · How we are paid</span><h2 id="fee-h">Disclosed plainly.</h2></div>
    <div class="right prose">
      <p>Statecraft Systems may be paid an introducer or referral fee by the buyer (micro1 or other licensees such as Polyshares). We are never paid by the seller. We refer a company only with its consent, and we never receive or hold the data itself.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap split" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <div class="left"><span class="eyebrow">05 · Questions</span><h2 id="faq-h">Before you decide.</h2></div>
    <div class="right prose records-faq">
      <h3>Will my clients know?</h3>
      <p>Client names and identifying details are removed or the records are excluded. We also check whether your contracts require notice or consent. Redaction is not a reason to skip those obligations; if a record cannot be shared safely and lawfully, it stays out.</p>
      <h3>Who sees it?</h3>
      <p>The buyer you sign with, such as micro1 or another licensee like Polyshares. Before you agree, the contract must specify the recipients, permitted uses and access controls. Statecraft never receives, holds or views the records themselves; they move only between you and the buyer.</p>
      <h3>What does it pay?</h3>
      <p><a class="link-rule" href="https://www.micro1.ai/data-estimate">micro1 publishes partnership tiers of $100K+, $500K+ and $1M+</a>, agreed with the buyer deal by deal. The actual price depends on the records: their quality, uniqueness, volume and the agreed access terms. Those tiers are not a quote or a promise of payment for your records.</p>
      <h3>Can I stop?</h3>
      <p>You can stop the review before signing, with no obligation. After signing, withdrawal, termination and any continued use of delivered records depend on the contract. We review those terms with you before delivery; do not assume a completed license can be undone.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="big">Most of our work is building the systems small institutions run on. This is the same knowledge, put to a second use.</p>
      <a class="link-rule" href="mailto:m@statecraft.systems?subject=Records%20review">Book a 20-minute records review</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
